{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/331302-exalted-2-5-five-dragon-force-blow-another-annoying-idiotic-question","id":331302,"title":"[Exalted 2.5] Five-Dragon Force Blow - another annoying idiotic question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-05T10:56:20-08:00","id":331302,"title":"[Exalted 2.5] Five-Dragon Force Blow - another annoying idiotic question","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;This attack doubles the normal base damage from an attack (which does not include extra successes) before subtracting soak&quot; <b>- Manual of Exalted Power: Dragon-Blooded, pg. 190</b> </div> </div> </div>...Ahhhh, ooooookay... So...You forgo extra successes entirely and simply double the base damage, subtract soak and apply that <i>without the extra successes at all</i>? I got that right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T11:16:07-08:00","id":331337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/331302-exalted-2-5-five-dragon-force-blow-another-annoying-idiotic-question#post331302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...Ahhhh, ooooookay... So...You forgo extra successes entirely and simply double the base damage, subtract soak and apply that <i>without the extra successes at all</i>? I got that right?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you double the base damage and then add successes. It's a weaker version of Hungry Tiger Technique in this regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T14:40:34-08:00","id":331501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a weaker version of Hungry Tiger Technique in this regard. </div> </div> </div>Mmmm, I'm actually unsure of this. I'd say it's a bit more situational.<br /> If you're a Dragon Blood and you have a Base Damage of 10L (Strength 4 with a Jade Dire Lance, say - a form weapon for this Style) and you double that, you get 20 damage dice before adding to those your extra successes, subtracting soak, etc. It seems fairly powerful if you just-barely hit something that doesn't have a huge Soak pool (like a Hobgoblin with a lethal soak of 5 or a heroic mortal with 4-7 soak or so), <br /> <br /> Hungry Tiger Technique doubles your extra successes - which is great when you have those and they stick around past the target's DV. It's less fun when the DV eats most of them away, leaving you with 2-4 extra damage dice in place of the whopping 20 in the above Dragon-Blood example.<br /> <br /> Seems to me like this is actually one of the few places where a Dragon-Blood charm can actually give a Solar charm a run for its essence motes or at least keep up and not collapse in the middle of the race and vanish in the dust.<br /> Hungry Tiger is great if you combo it with 2nd Excellency and catch an opponent with a depleted DV (and no Charms that restore it in response to your attack), Five-Dragon Force Blow is great if you strike an opponent that may have a high DV which you pass-but-just-barely but not much in the way of Soak. <br /> The same Low-Soak-But-High-DV target would nearly nullify Hungry Tiger if it negates most of the extra successes (and assuming the same 9L base damage as the Dragon-Blood's, most of the dice would get chopped off into near-nothing by even a fairly meager Soak like the Hobgoblin's). <br /> <br /> That's what I understand, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T06:42:23-08:00","id":334165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/331302-exalted-2-5-five-dragon-force-blow-another-annoying-idiotic-question?p=331501#post331501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mmmm, I'm actually unsure of this. I'd say it's a bit more situational.<br /> If you're a Dragon Blood and you have a Base Damage of 10L (Strength 4 with a Jade Dire Lance, say - a form weapon for this Style) and you double that, you get 20 damage dice before adding to those your extra successes, subtracting soak, etc. It seems fairly powerful if you just-barely hit something that doesn't have a huge Soak pool (like a Hobgoblin with a lethal soak of 5 or a heroic mortal with 4-7 soak or so),<br /> <br /> Hungry Tiger Technique doubles your extra successes - which is great when you have those and they stick around past the target's DV. It's less fun when the DV eats most of them away, leaving you with 2-4 extra damage dice in place of the whopping 20 in the above Dragon-Blood example.<br /> <br /> Seems to me like this is actually one of the few places where a Dragon-Blood charm can actually give a Solar charm a run for its essence motes or at least keep up and not collapse in the middle of the race and vanish in the dust.<br /> Hungry Tiger is great if you combo it with 2nd Excellency and catch an opponent with a depleted DV (and no Charms that restore it in response to your attack), Five-Dragon Force Blow is great if you strike an opponent that may have a high DV which you pass-but-just-barely but not much in the way of Soak.<br /> The same Low-Soak-But-High-DV target would nearly nullify Hungry Tiger if it negates most of the extra successes (and assuming the same 9L base damage as the Dragon-Blood's, most of the dice would get chopped off into near-nothing by even a fairly meager Soak like the Hobgoblin's).<br /> <br /> That's what I understand, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just typing up something very similar.<br /> <br /> It's also ambiguous as to whether Supplemental Charms that boost damage like Falling Star Manoeuvre have their effects doubled. Even without that, it's possible for a Dragon-Blood to have a base damage in the low 20s. Five Dragon Force Blow is not a well designed Charm.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T17:45:04-08:00","id":334687,"title":"","content":"I think they don't, because it does say Base Damage.<br /> <br /> But even without them, this is honestly a brutally good charm. I've seen PCs accidentally kill other PCs with this charm because it's so good for 2m and the PC who used it thought &quot;it's just a 2m charm, it'll be fine&quot;. I've used this charm to have a base damage of over 50 before.<br /> It's only weakness is that it's Simple so can't be used in a flurry, and considering how good it is that's a very good thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T17:48:45-08:00","id":334700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/331302-exalted-2-5-five-dragon-force-blow-another-annoying-idiotic-question?p=334687#post334687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they don't, because it does say Base Damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it goes on to define Base Damage as excluding threshold successes. I'm in favour of nerfing it as much as is reasonable, but like I said, it's ambiguous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/331302-exalted-2-5-five-dragon-force-blow-another-annoying-idiotic-question?p=334687#post334687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But even without them, this is honestly a brutally good charm. I've seen PCs accidentally kill other PCs with this charm because it's so good for 2m and the PC who used it thought &quot;it's just a 2m charm, it'll be fine&quot;. I've used this charm to have a base damage of over 50 before.</div> </div> </div> </div>When in doubt, always use Coup De Grace.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/331302-exalted-2-5-five-dragon-force-blow-another-annoying-idiotic-question?p=334687#post334687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's only weakness is that it's Simple so can't be used in a flurry, and considering how good it is that's a very good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless it's used in an Extra Action Charm... like the one in Five Dragon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T18:01:04-08:00","id":334710,"title":"","content":"You want to know what's fucked up? Use Glorious Birthright Font, Five Dragon Claw and Five Dragon Force Blow. You're spending like 5 motes on an attack with a base damage of 32 and a boat load of added effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T18:32:21-08:00","id":334714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/331302-exalted-2-5-five-dragon-force-blow-another-annoying-idiotic-question?p=334710#post334710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You want to know what's fucked up? Use Glorious Birthright Font, Five Dragon Claw and Five Dragon Force Blow. You're spending like 5 motes on an attack with a base damage of 32 and a boat load of added effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can also use that one Resistance Charm to increase damage with Jade weapons by 5 for the action. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T20:28:06-08:00","id":334784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/331302-exalted-2-5-five-dragon-force-blow-another-annoying-idiotic-question?p=334700#post334700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it goes on to define Base Damage as excluding threshold successes. I'm in favour of nerfing it as much as is reasonable, but like I said, it's ambiguous.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, I'll admit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unless it's used in an Extra Action Charm... like the one in Five Dragon. </div> </div> </div>Indeed! Luckily, in my experience people just buy Five-Dragon Claw and Five-Dragon Force Blow most of the time, but you can combine it for some truly horrific effects.<br /> Of course, this is the style that also includes making your fist do agg, and allows you to bounce a mountain off your head (unless someone spent a mote to throw the mountain of course).<br /> People say TMA are supposed to be weaker than DB native charms. I don't think anyone told the writer of Five Dragon style.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T05:52:08-08:00","id":335068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/331302-exalted-2-5-five-dragon-force-blow-another-annoying-idiotic-question?p=334784#post334784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People say TMA are supposed to be weaker than DB native charms. I don't think anyone told the writer of Five Dragon style.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a reason for that! <br /> <br /> Five Dragon Style is copypasted from the 1e native Dragon-Blood Martial Arts tree. (Terrestrial Hero was Dragon-Blood Brawl.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T06:28:52-08:00","id":335105,"title":"","content":"Ah, that makes sense. I knew Terrestrial Hero was Brawl, I didn't know Five-Dragon was MA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T23:49:26-08:00","id":335873,"title":"","content":"Jon Chung did an interesting rewrite of Five Dragon style on the old forum. not sure if anyone still has a copy kicking around...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/999-winterstar","name":"Winterstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar999_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T14:52:23-08:00","id":336331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-